  "final_message": "Refunding a paid invoice should now work. The full test suite passes (24 tests), but I didn't add a test that reproduces the refund failure.\n\n**Root cause:** `refund_invoice` in `billing/refunds.py` called `successful_payments(ctx, invoice[\"customer_id\"])`. That function takes an invoice id and looks up payments for that invoice. Passing the customer id found no payments, so nothing was refunded and the \"no successful payment to refund\" error was raised.\n\n**Fix:** it now calls `successful_payments(ctx, invoice_id)`.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repository root: `{\"file\": \"refunds.py\", \"function\": \"refund_invoice\"}`.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
